ROCR-Runtime (re-diffed for pinned commit 2b22ab0195cc1461cd9abf3b969e9dd7c10af350,
therock-7.14 / ROCm 7.14.0, from the shipped fix against rocm-6.4.4,
gfx803/patches/rocr/va-reuse-defer.patch): stop immediate GPU virtual-address
(VA) recycling in libhsakmt's fmm aperture allocator, which corrupts MIOpen
CK reduction kernels on gfx803 (Polaris), by parking freed objects alive on
a length-bounded FIFO and freeing them only at GPU-busy flush points; and
default the hsa-runtime SimpleHeap fragment sub-allocator to OFF, since it
is a second, higher-layer VA recycler that the fmm fix cannot see.

See gfx803/patches/rocr/va-reuse-defer.patch for the full WHY (root-cause
investigation, rejected non-solutions, hardware validation numbers) --
unchanged in substance from 6.4.4, reproduced here only for the WHAT and
the re-diff.

