WHAT
----
Same mechanism as gfx803/patches/rocr/va-reuse-defer.patch: at
hsakmt_fmm_release, the object is parked on a per-aperture FIFO, fully
alive (BOs kept, GPU mapping untouched, VA reserved, content intact).
When the entry ages out (FIFO > FMM_REUSE_QUEUE_MAX=256 entries or >
FMM_REUSE_BYTES_MAX=1GiB parked bytes) it is really freed inside a LATER
FREE call -- i.e. while the GPU pipeline is typically active, the measured
stale-clearing ingredient -- then the VA returns to the aperture
free-list. Scratch apertures bypass the FIFO to keep
fmm_release_scratch's exit loop terminating. HSA_DISABLE_FRAGMENT_ALLOCATOR
defaults to disabling the fragment sub-allocator (set it to "0" to
re-enable), since that allocator recycles VAs above libhsakmt where the
fmm-level fix cannot see it.
